From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: a failed pipeline cache write no longer deletes the whole cache file, and out of memory while reading no longer cuts it (after Lichii #815), EDEN_UP_CACHE_KEEP_GOOD=1, off by default

What: SerializePipeline deleted the whole pipeline cache file (or the mesh one) when a record could
not be written (a full disk), and also when the file could not be opened: the failbit is armed
before the open test, so the failed open throws and the catch deletes the file. Then the next
start has no cached pipelines: a cold start, first-sight stutter everywhere.

With the switch, in this core patch (shader_environment.cpp, SerializePipeline):
- a file that cannot be opened is left alone (one error line);
- a record that could not be written whole is cut off again (the file goes back to its size before
  the record), so the next record follows complete records;
- appends take a process-wide mutex (one writer thread today; cheap).

The reading side: the PS5 build does not use LoadPipelines from this file. headless/CMakeLists.txt
replaces it with headless/shader_cache_reader.inc, which already keeps the entries before a damaged
one and cuts the file back to them (the main part of upstream #815, done here earlier). The same
commit as this patch file changes that reader, with the same switch:
- out of memory while reading stops the reading and keeps the file whole (before: the file was cut
  back to the entry being read, so every entry after it was lost though nothing was damaged);
  line "[EglantinePS5] shader cache: no memory while reading <file> after n bytes; reading stopped,
  the file is kept whole (EDEN_UP_CACHE_KEEP_GOOD)";
- the sixth size of each environment (constant buffer replacements) is checked too, before
  anything is allocated for it;
- a compute entry must hold one environment, a graphics entry no compute one.

Not taken from upstream (much bigger, on code we do not have): the file lock between emulators (one
emulator per console), the rewrite that removes stale or duplicate records, host-property tags,
deeper per-environment checks, the tests.

Switch: EDEN_UP_CACHE_KEEP_GOOD=1 (exact "1"), read once (core and reader read it each on their
own). Off: one test of a static bool, then the old code in both places.

Price: none in play. This changes the PS5 build's derived shader_environment.cpp, which is an input
of tools/gen-translation-id.py: with EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SOURCE_STAMP=1 the first boot of this build
starts a new shader store (like any build that changes translation inputs).

Test: normal starts should load the same pipeline count. The write part shows only on a full disk
or a file that cannot be opened (the old code's delete would be followed by a cold next start). Not
checked: a run.

Origin and credit: Zortos, zortos293/Lichii cfa85c12b4 (#815), "video_core, vulkan: drop only damaged,
stale or duplicate pipeline cache records"; the write part is his code (without the lock), the
reader changes follow his load code (bad_alloc keeps the file; the stage checks).
